sc: the idle timer sleeps when nothing is left to do

ScModule's idle timer climbs from 150 ms to 3000 ms and then fires
every three seconds for as long as Calc runs, with no document work.
Ely keeps a Calc engine waiting from login: it woke 22 times in ten
minutes with nothing to do (Ely SF.23).

At 3000 ms with no link or text-width work left, the handler no
longer restarts the timer. AnythingChanged, called on every change
and on every new visible range, starts it again at 150 ms.

diff --git a/sc/source/ui/app/scmod.cxx b/sc/source/ui/app/scmod.cxx
index d9d11e1..9145655 100644
--- a/sc/source/ui/app/scmod.cxx
+++ b/sc/source/ui/app/scmod.cxx
@@ -1916,6 +1916,9 @@ void ScModule::AnythingChanged()
         m_aIdleTimer.SetTimeout( SC_IDLE_MIN );
 
     nIdleCount = 0;
+    // A stopped timer wakes on change.
+    if ( !m_aIdleTimer.IsActive() )
+        m_aIdleTimer.Start();
 }
 
 static void lcl_CheckNeedsRepaint( const ScDocShell* pDocShell )
@@ -1980,7 +1983,9 @@ IMPL_LINK_NOARG(ScModule, IdleHandler, Timer *, void)
     if ( nNewTime != nOldTime )
         m_aIdleTimer.SetTimeout( nNewTime );
 
-
+    // Nothing left: sleep until AnythingChanged.
+    if ( !bMore && nOldTime == SC_IDLE_MAX )
+        return;
     m_aIdleTimer.Start();
 }
 
